# Pulse Desk — sectors linkage & load rules

Live URL: `https://us-market-pulse-6sqa.onrender.com/sectors`

## Required linkages (do not break)

Clicking the **right pulse ranking** (`[data-pulse-sector]`) must synchronously update:

1. Rank active state (聚焦)
2. Left **个股强弱与推荐** (`sector_pulse.stock_desk`)
3. Bottom **成分股** list + first/selected symbol chart / news / chain
4. URL `?sector=&symbol=`

Other links that must stay wired:

- Map tile / sector label → `openSectorDesk`
- Pulse stock card → `selectSectorSymbol` (bottom desk)
- Horizon tabs (一周～四周) → re-render ranking for that horizon; keep active sector stock desk linked
- US markets strip/futures TF switches must not blank a painted block

## Map 1w–4w (keep)

- Server: `fill_horizon`, merge `_MAP_RET_CACHE` on timeout, background horizon fill
- Client: quiet `fillHorizon` (never `force` wipe treemap for sparse weeks)
- Session restore of `sectorMap` / `sectorMapTf`

## Loading / cache guardrails

- Empty timeout stubs (`sectors: []`, `strip: []`, `picks: []`) must **never** wipe already-painted UI
- Lite / unquoted shells (`change_pct` sparse) are **not** warm cache — do not short-circuit rank clicks on them
- Prefer `paintLinkedSectorDesk` (or equivalent) so rank + stock desk + picks paint on the same tick
- Prefetch and soft desk load share one inflight key (`soft:<sectorId>`), timeout ≥ server budget (~20s)
- Stuck "正在切换…" is a bug — use local stock-desk fallback + watchdog recovery

## Revert / version policy

- Do **not** revert linkage/stub fixes just to keep map week fills — keep **both**
- When changing sectors UI/load paths, manually verify: rank click → left desk + 成分股 + chart update within one interaction
- Bump `base.html` `?v=` and `sw.js` cache together after FE changes

## Key files

- `src/us_market_pulse/static/app.js` — `openSectorDesk`, `paintLinkedSectorDesk`, `loadSectorDesk`, `loadSectorMap`, `renderSectorPulse`
- `src/us_market_pulse/market_map.py` — horizon returns / fill
- `src/us_market_pulse/sectors.py` — desk + peek cache
- `src/us_market_pulse/app.py` — `/api/sectors`, `/api/sectors/map`, `/api/us-markets` budgets
